  "slug": "microbe-comprehensive-mapping-583d",
  "summary": "Remote sequence and structural comparisons now assign function to proteins beyond Pfam and ECOD coverage.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extending functional annotation of proteins beyond the coverage of standard family databases. A bioinformatic pipeline infers functions for hypothetical proteins of Rickettsia akari, a reduced-genome obligate intracellular pathogen, nominating virulence-associated and effector candidates. HMM-HMM comparisons across 5,396 phage genomes yield 13,035 conserved fragments that annotate 50% of phage proteins beyond Pfam and ECOD. DaliScope addresses downstream interpretation by distilling complete DALI structural-alignment target sets through community detection and Pfam annotation. The IEDB 2026 update and the HLA peptide-binding motif framework fall outside bacterial genomics but similarly organize large datasets into standardized or grouped functional categories. What is new is the reliance on remote sequence and structural similarity to assign function beyond Pfam and ECOD coverage.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-16"
}
